        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Shoma Morita, Melanie Reizes Klein\n- Therapies and Theories: Morita therapy, object relations theory\n- Topics: psychoanalysis, child psychology\n\nFacts:\n- Shoma Morita created Morita therapy through case-based research.\n- Shoma Morita lived from 1874 to 1938 and was an M.D.\n- Morita therapy is an ecological, purpose-centered, response-oriented therapy.\n- Melanie Reizes Klein lived from 30 March 1882 to 22 September 1960.\n- Melanie Reizes Klein was an Austrian-British psychoanalyst.\n- Melanie Reizes Klein devised novel therapeutic techniques for children.\n- Melanie Reizes Klein's techniques influenced child psychology and contemporary psychoanalysis.\n- Melanie Reizes Klein was a leading innovator in object relations theory.",
